  "raw_text": "59\n\nDamra\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDara\n\nDan/Dah\nn\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDan\nh\n\nDanh\n \n(\ndictu,t34,km,ll,my,jl,fy,bm,fg\n; a/t:\n \nDan\n-\nkt,my,bh,lv\n;\n \nDahn\n-\ndict\n) (adj,adv)\n \n–\n \ndone, finished, stop, stopped\n \n/ hecho,\nterminado, detente, detenido\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nDanh sa\n \n–\n \nit is done\n \n/ se hace\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh8\n):\n \nupla ailal ba dan makabi walras\n \n–\n \nmany people are done asking questions\n \n/ mucha gente ha terminado de hacer\n\npreguntas\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh9\n):\n \nupla ailal baha ansika nani ba dan plikras\n \n–\n \nmany people have\n \nstopped looking for th\no\nse answers\n \n/ muchas personas\n\nhan dejado de buscar esas respuestas\n)\n\nDanh âpu kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be done and gone, to be finished and not having now\n \n/ estar acabado y desaparecido,\nestar terminado y no tener ahora\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \npât wahwanka ba danh âpu kabia\n \n–\n \nsuffering will be done and gone\n \n/ el sufrimiento se acabará y se irá)\n\nDanh daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto complete, to finish\n \n/ completar, terminar\n\nDanh\n \nâpu\n \ndaukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cause to be gone, to eliminate\n \n/ hacer desaparecer, eliminar\n\nDanh munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto complete, to finish\n \n/ completar, terminar\n\nDanh sauhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto destroy and make gone, to completely destroy\n \n/ destruir y desaparecer, destruir\ncompletamente\n\nDanh swapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give up, to tire out\n \n/ rendirse, cansarse\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKupia swapaia\n)\n\nDanh swiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stop and leave, to finish and leave\n \n/ pararse y irse, terminar y salir\n\nDanh takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to be finished, to come to completion\n \n/ llegar a ser terminado, para llegar a su fin\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/19\n):\n \nSiknis nani sut ba yu kum dahn takbia ki?\n \n–\n \nWill there come to be a day when all sicknesses are done?\n\n/ ¿Llegará el día en que todas las enfermedades terminen?)\n\nDanh\n \nâ\npu takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cease to exist\n \n/ dejar de existir\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh58\n):\n \nUpla kum pruya taim, dan\n \nâ\npu takisa\n \n–\n \nWhen a person dies, (they) cease to exist\n \n/ Cuando una\n\npersona muere, (ellos) dejan de existir\n)\n\nDanh takaia bîla nani ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nconcluding words, words to finish\n \n/ palabras finales, palabras para\nterminar\n\nSut danh\n \n–\n \nall finished\n \n/ todo terminado\n\nDaniel\n \n(\ndb,dbta,bw\n;\n \nDanyal\n-dba\n)\n \n–\n \nDaniel\n \n(Bible book) / Daniel (libro bíblico)\n\nDans\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndance\n \n/ baile\n\nDans daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make a dance\n \n/ hacer un baile\n\nDans pulaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto dance\n \n/ bailar\n\nDapna\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nson-in-law, father-in-law\n \n/ yerno, suegro\n\n(Construct:\n \nDaipna\n;\n \nDampra\n;\n \nDapnika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-17\n):\n \nDîa muni yang wari takaia apia sna muli yapti bara daipna ba maritki lâka dukiara uba luki ba mita?\n \n–\n \nWhy\n\nshouldn’t I worry that my mother\n-in-law and my father-in-law are thinking a lot about (interested in) my marriage?\n \n/ ¿Por qué no\ndebería preocuparme que mi suegra y mi suegro estén pensando mucho (interesados) en mi matrimonio?)\n\nDara\n \n(\ndict,dictu;\n \nDahra\n-dict-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nfeeling\n \n/ sentimiento\n\n(Construct:\n \nDaihra/Daira\n;\n \nDamra/Damhra\n)\n\nDara walaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDahra walaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \nfeel, to perceive, to be conscious, to be aware, to be thoughtful, to be\ninexperienced (db-Lawana Nani 19:7)\n \n/ sentir, percibir, ser consciente, ser reflexivo, ser inexperto\n \n(db-Lawana\nNani 19:7)\n\n(Construct:\n \nDaira\n \n(a/t:\n \nDaihra\n)\n \nwalisna\n \n–\n \nI feel, I am aware...\n \n/ Siento, soy consciente...;\n \nDamra\n \n(a/t:\n \nDamhra\n)\n \nwalisma\n \n–\n\nyou feel, you are aware...\n \n/ sientes, eres consciente...)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Smasmalkra 9:5\n):\n \nraya nani ba ai dahra walisa, witin nani pruaia ba\n \n–\n \nthe living are conscious they (are) to die\n \n/\nlos vivos son conscientes de que deben morir)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n06/19\n):\n \nIlayas nahki ai dara walan?\n \n–\n \nHow\n \ndid Elijah feel?\n \n/ ¿Cómo se sintió Elijah?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg2\n):\n \nNaha wauhkataya hilp mai munbia Baibil stadi takisma taim, kau lilia damra walaia.\n \n–\n \nThis brochure will help\n\nyou to feel more happy when you study the Bible.\n \n/ Este folleto lo ayudará a\n \nsentirse más feliz cuando estudie la Biblia.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \nYawan nahki nu sa G\nȃ\nd ba ai t\nȃ\nnka brisa nahki wan dara wali ba?\n \n–\n \nHow do we know that God has\n\nunderstanding of (understands) how we are feeling?\n \n/ Cómo sabemos que Dios tiene comprensión de (comprende) cómo\n\nnos sentimos?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nNahki âmyapah damra walaia sip sma?\n \n–\n \nHow can you feel satisfied?\n \n/ ¿Cómo puedes sentirte satisfecho?)\n\nDara walanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nDahra walanka\n,\n \nDara lukanka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfeeling\n \n/ sentimiento",
